# No `git push` unless explicitly requested

## Requirement

- **Never** run `git push`, `git push -u`, or any remote publish unless the user **clearly asks** in that turn (e.g. "push", "ارفع جيت", "push to origin").
- Do **not** push "to complete" a task, verify CI, or sync after commits unless asked.
- Commits only when requested — see user commit rules.

## Allowed without push

```bash
git status
git diff
git log
git add … && git commit …   # only when user asked to commit
```
